      "writtenOn": "2025-06-11T23:45:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My gut is telling me that we should probably just be serializing the `ToggleState`/`ToggleSet` from the device instead of individual toggle `bool`s here. If we can use `ToggleSet`, it wouldn\u0027t be too bad in terms of space since it\u0027s just a bitset, but it would be a LOT more future-proof for when we add new features and stuff.\n\nOtherwise, anytime we add a new toggle we potentially would need to add another `bool` here if we check it when parsing the shader.\n\nI\u0027m on the fence w.r.t serializing the related `FeaturesSet` also, but I\u0027m thinking that maybe it\u0027s better to do that for future-proofing also.\n\nJust as a side-note to make my point stronger, I think the device cache key (used in the frontend cache) also already serializes the entire `FeaturesSet` and `TogglesSet`, so I think that is probably the way to go for this.",
